    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1491">

                <pb facs="0964" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/107b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Edwards.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Unofficially call upon de facto authorities in Juarez in company with two
                    witnesses whose standing will likely cause you to receive the highest
                    consideration, and if convenient take Zach Cobb with you. Request to see the
                    body of Benton and if granted take accurate note of every detail of its
                    condition.</p>
                <p>If previous burial makes granting of request impossible ask to be shown where
                    body is interred, if possible have witnesses accompany you to the spot and take
                    such observations as will enable grave to be unmistakably located.</p>
                <pb facs="0965" n="849" xml:id="pg849"/>
                <p>Secure written statement regarding condition of Benton’s body after death, from
                    undertaker who embalmed it, from those who prepared it for burial or interred
                    it, or from any and all available witnesses.</p>
                <p>Department expects your report already mailed will embrace every detail
                    available, wishes telegraphic answer as to the result of above representations
                    and to know just what efforts you have made and are making to get written
                    statements from responsible sources.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
